######## 77. Leaving an app out, and clearing what a removed project left

-- a name that is no app's is said before anything is written

$ kagebunshin onboard depot --exclude apps/old
kagebunshin: --exclude apps/old names no app, by its folder or its project's name; nothing was written; the apps there are $T/work/depot/apps/back (depot-back), $T/work/depot/apps/front (depot-front), $T/work/depot/apps/legacy (depot-legacy)
[exit 2]

-- the apps are listed before the passphrase; the one left out gets no project and no section

(human) $ kagebunshin onboard depot --exclude apps/legacy
onboarding 2 apps in 1 checkout: 2 env files to import
  apps/back: import .env into new project depot-back
  apps/front: import .env into new project depot-front
  apps/legacy: left out
Passphrase for the local store (to import 2 .env files): 
importing $T/work/depot/apps/back/.env into [depot-back.dev]
importing $T/work/depot/apps/front/.env into [depot-front.dev]
writing 2 keys from 2 files to the local store
reading the state of depot-back (1 of 2)
reading the state of depot-front (2 of 2)

depot-back ($T/work/depot/apps/back): created project depot-back with environment dev, and put 1 key from .env in the local store's [depot-back.dev]: API_TOKEN
  environment dev: 1 of 1 keys set
  ready: your agent proves it with a run

depot-front ($T/work/depot/apps/front): created project depot-front with environment dev, and put 1 key from .env in the local store's [depot-front.dev]: API_TOKEN
  environment dev: 1 of 1 keys set
  ready: your agent proves it with a run

skipped $T/work/depot/apps/legacy: left out with --exclude

Then, in each checkout above that is not done, paste this line into your coding agent:
  Set up kagebunshin here: run `kagebunshin next` and do what it says until it says done.

Delete $T/work/depot/apps/back/.env, $T/work/depot/apps/front/.env now that their values are in the store? [y/N] kept $T/work/depot/apps/back/.env, $T/work/depot/apps/front/.env; delete them once `kagebunshin run -- COMMAND` works

$ kagebunshin store list | grep depot
[depot-back.dev]
[depot-front.dev]

-- it stays out: `next` does not wait for it, and the checkout drafted again passes over it

$ kagebunshin next
this repository has 3 apps, each its own project
  apps/back: project depot-back, environment dev: 1 of 1 keys set, not yet proven
  apps/front: project depot-front, environment dev: 1 of 1 keys set, not yet proven
  apps/legacy: left out; `kagebunshin onboard` of its folder sets it up
next (you): in apps/back: prove the setup: run the project's tests or its start command with its keys; pick the command
  cd apps/back && kagebunshin run --strict -- COMMAND

$ kagebunshin project draft --apply
draft of project depot-back for apps/back:
  $T/work/depot/apps/back/.env has values and nothing else says where its secrets live, so nothing was drafted; `onboard` moves them into kagebunshin, with a person's approval
      kagebunshin onboard $T/work/depot   (human)
draft of project depot-front for apps/front:
  $T/work/depot/apps/front/.env has values and nothing else says where its secrets live, so nothing was drafted; `onboard` moves them into kagebunshin, with a person's approval
      kagebunshin onboard $T/work/depot   (human)
note: left out, as `kagebunshin onboard --exclude` said: apps/legacy; `kagebunshin onboard DIR` sets one up

$ ls $HOME/.config/kagebunshin/projects | grep depot
depot-back.toml
depot-front.toml

-- a project removed leaves its values in the store, and says how to clear them

$ kagebunshin project remove depot-back
removed project depot-back ($T/home/.config/kagebunshin/projects/depot-back.toml)
its values are still in the local store: [depot-back.dev] (1 key)
to remove them, run `kagebunshin store clear depot-back` in a terminal; it asks for the passphrase

-- clearing is refused while the project is there, and takes the passphrase: a person's

$ kagebunshin store clear depot-front
kagebunshin: project depot-front is still there, and its environments read these values; nothing was removed
hint: `kagebunshin project remove depot-front` removes the project; `kagebunshin store unset SECTION KEY` removes one key
[exit 5]

$ kagebunshin --json store clear depot-back
this removes [depot-back.dev] (1 key) from the local store
{"code":"no_terminal","message":"cannot read a passphrase from the terminal: No such device or address (os error 6)","hint":"run this in an interactive terminal","who":"human","tell":"Please run `kagebunshin store clear depot-back` in a terminal; it asks for the store passphrase and removes the values project depot-back left in the local store."}
[exit 1]

(human) $ kagebunshin store clear depot-back
this removes [depot-back.dev] (1 key) from the local store
Passphrase for the local store: 
removed [depot-back.dev] (1 key)

$ kagebunshin store list | grep depot
[depot-front.dev]
